{
  "$schema": "../spec.schema.json",
  "title": "Okta as the source of truth for workforce identity",
  "description": "Okta is the source of truth for workforce identity. Okta takes in each person's profile and job details from HR over HTTPS 443, uses Active Directory in several domains and forests as a source, links each person's AD accounts by employee ID and creates, updates and disables AD accounts and groups in the right domain and OU. Group rules give day-one access and Okta signs users in to SAML and OIDC applications and provisions them over SCIM, removing access when people move or leave. Okta Access Gateway adds Okta sign-in and MFA to on-premises web applications, LDAP applications look up users through the LDAP Interface and send updates to Okta or Active Directory and APIs accept Okta access tokens and check their scopes and claims. Native Kerberos applications, such as file shares and SQL Server, sign users in with Windows Kerberos and Okta provisions the AD accounts and groups they use. Okta signs people in to SAML and OIDC, on-premises web and LDAP applications with AD checking the password, context-aware authentication checks device, network and risk at sign-in and during the session, Identity Governance runs access requests and reviews, Workflows runs custom logic and event-driven automation and returns changes since their last check to self-provisioning applications, read from Okta and the System Log and the SIEM reads Okta's System Log.",
